# Sentinel automation invariants

Apply whenever creating or editing files under `automation/**/*.py`.

1. **Scripts never assign verdicts.** Do not set Public Assessment, Internal Validity, or Duplicate Analysis in code, defaults, or generated platform answers. Those fields are human-only.
2. **Never invent rewards.** Do not fabricate oracle `1.0`, NOP `0.0`, or any Harbor reward/timing. Record only values from real local or platform runs (or leave unset / null).
3. **Absolute paths.** Prefer absolute paths for ZIPs, task roots, repos, and script invocations so cwd mistakes cannot silently retarget another session.
4. **`--task-name` when ambiguous.** If more than one `work/<task>/` (or equivalent) session could match, require or pass `--task-name <exact>` — never guess.

Related: `CLAUDE.md` Safety, `AGENTS.md` Must, `docs/EXECUTION_LAYER.md`.
